diagnosis_text:
Affected component: OSPF on the distribution switches’ management SVI (br0.99). Mechanism: dswa1 and dswb1 are sending OSPF hellos on VLAN 99 with a /32 netmask, while their neighbors expect /28. Those hellos are rejected as “NetworkMask mismatch,” causing repeated OSPF control-plane churn and occasional brief stalls seen campus-wide.

Localization: 
- dswa1 br0.99 has two IPs: 10.0.0.2/28 and 10.0.0.1/32 (ip -br addr show br0.99).
- dswb1 br0.99 has 10.0.0.18/28 and 10.0.0.17/32.
